IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`

-- P9-gate: three thin gates for the provisions of part P9 (Articles 80 to 112), each a call of the keel's one
-- applicability function `Art 113 the provision group applies` with the provision group fixed.
-- It restates no date of Article 113 or Article 111 and writes no applicability test of its own: it only names
-- the group (PLAN.md section 3: "which provision group is a provision in?") so that a layer-1 module of P9 does
-- not repeat five arguments on every function.
--   Articles 80 to 98, Article 101 and Article 112                 the group General (the general date of application)
--   Articles 99 and 100                                            the group `Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78`
--   Articles 102 to 110                                            the group `Articles 102 to 110`
-- A gate answers FALSE for "does not apply on the date asked" (not yet, or saved by Article 111(2)); the caller
-- answers NOTHING, never JUST FALSE (PLAN.md section 5; keel fork F-111-2-nothing).
-- A gate "to the AI system" passes the system's route, placement date and design change to the keel's function, so
-- that Article 111(2)'s saving of a high-risk AI system placed on the market earlier is applied. A gate with no AI
-- system passes the core's constants (the route and date "to pass when no AI system is in question") and FALSE.

§ `Articles 80 to 98, 101 and 112: the group General`

GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` MEANS
    `Art 113 the provision group applies` General `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE

GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies to the AI system` MEANS
    `Art 113 the provision group applies` General `the date asked` (`the AI system`'s `route`) (`the AI system`'s `date placed on the market or put into service`) (`the AI system`'s `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)

§ `Articles 99 and 100: the group of Chapter III Section 4, Chapters V, VII and XII and Article 78`

GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Arts 99 and 100 the group Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78 applies` MEANS
    `Art 113 the provision group applies` `Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78` `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE

GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Arts 99 and 100 the group Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78 applies to the AI system` MEANS
    `Art 113 the provision group applies` `Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78` `the date asked` (`the AI system`'s `route`) (`the AI system`'s `date placed on the market or put into service`) (`the AI system`'s `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)

-- The group of the provisions that Article 99(4)(a) to (e) names (Articles 16, 22, 23, 24, 25 and 26: Chapter III Section 3).
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 99(4) the group Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 applies to the AI system` MEANS
    `Art 113 the provision group applies` `Chapter III Sections 1 to 3` `the date asked` (`the AI system`'s `route`) (`the AI system`'s `date placed on the market or put into service`) (`the AI system`'s `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)

§ `Articles 102 to 110: the group Articles 102 to 110`

GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Arts 102 to 110 the group Articles 102 to 110 applies` MEANS
    `Art 113 the provision group applies` `Articles 102 to 110` `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE

-- Article 99(4)(g) fines non-compliance with the transparency obligations of Article 50 (Chapter IV, the group General).
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 99(4)(g) the group General applies to the AI system for Article 50` MEANS
    `Art 113 the provision group applies` General `the date asked` (`the AI system`'s `route`) (`the AI system`'s `date placed on the market or put into service`) (`the AI system`'s `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
